{"body":"Slice T43, canonical `patches-unshipped`, M6.P2 under area epic #1054. Run the coordinator's proved `docs/reviews/briefs/patches-unshipped.md` v2 under plan §6b. D-WORKFLOW-231 records scope, ownership and evidence. The explicit dispatch supplies the exact published seed/worktree/branch.\n\n## Scope\n\nExactly 432 vendor-carried path rows / 328,516 logical Git-blob lines: 346 Linux-source patches, 12 configurations, 74 other-source patches; 430 regular files and two symlinks. Zero fork-written/base-delta set. The table reads headers/targets/provenance/reachability and selected source inputs, not all 328,516 vendor body lines. All31 direct recipe contexts retain existing T25/T8/T30/T23/T11 owners. No source edit or removal.\n\nUnshipped is the inventory's path classification, not proof that no shipped consumer uses the bytes: T42's separately owned MangoHud link reaches a T43 referent. Config headers/static writers are not built configuration. T40/T41/T42 memberships stay separate. Local depth, actual primary identity, reviewers [].\n\nreviewed-at: 601e4694f9726b2228d3571efdb5cfc061c6d442\nfixed-at: 8282cbcade3be32b437f7391be7e216d9a6b1074\n\nCan this be done on the VM? No — this source-only table establishes immutable selection/provenance/application facts without runtime claims. No build, guest, config execution, fetch, provider/device/cloud action or host allocation. Missing optional cached inputs remain named open items; they grant no download or execution authority.\n\n## Acceptance criteria\n\n- [ ] 00–07, A–D receipts/tools and the one-file Local review-plan exist; no guest-cycle/build artifact.\n- [ ] Exact432 keys/328,516 logical lines, line/mode/link distinctions, zero fork-written and seed/source/P1 identity bindings verify with the helper.\n- [ ] Provenance and coverage each contain all432 unique keys and nonempty evidence/owner fields, with no invented whole-body reading.\n- [ ] The346 Linux patches/12 configs/74 other patches and72/31/28 directory/prefix/consumer groups reconcile without summing overlapping reach.\n- [ ] Both links and referents, executable modes and T42's separate shipped consumer retain exact identities/ownership; all neighboring membership intersections are empty.\n- [ ] All31 recipe contexts bind their actual conditional pins and existing owners; wrapper/source and module/kernel distinctions are correct.\n- [ ] The12 config rows separate source headers/static writers from built config/runtime; no config tool was executed.\n- [ ] Base and fixed651150fc88 currency statuses have exact source evidence; selector7.2.6 is not mislabeled source7.2.11, and integration owns moves/additions.\n- [ ] Every positive application has exact source/preimage/rendering/backend/stack/normal-result evidence; missing inputs remain specific open items. Partial-failure control refuses promotion and blocks successors.\n- [ ] All four table-generator negatives fail before its positive432-row output; program/input/output hashes and command exits are retained.\n- [ ] 03/04 cover conformance, doctrine, interactions/refutation and Q1–Q7, with classified proof/PROOF agreement and explicit unmeasured efficiency/time-to-play.\n- [ ] Actual primary/lab/identity source and historical identities are honest; Local reviewers[]/D-WORKFLOW-184, with no external-review claim.\n- [ ] Pre-issue lint and final normal/issue resolution lint print the appropriate PASS; each punch item reaches a recorded Phase-7 outcome with evidence/owner.\n- [ ] Bugs have trace, Already written, VM rationale and observable criteria; issue checks return0fail; unresolved bugs remain open.\n- [ ] Tree and per-commit guards protect all source/context/selector/rule/register paths and reject a planted source edit; no product or removal change.\n- [ ] Inherited and contribution rows retain exact owners/actions; #585 drafts remain unsent and class removal stays #1048/#346.\n- [ ] Closing census records no forbidden execution/allocation; owned source projections retire only after receipt custody is proved, caches preserved with the actual evidence strength stated.\n- [ ] Current rules/register/index/ceremony/forbidden/hooks and issue checks pass with real exits; final publication receipts bind the clean final tip.\n- [ ] Final posted retro and handback name one clean published tip, actual outcomes/friction/next owners and both untouched time-to-play quantities.\n- [ ] Live reviewed-at/fixed-at bind seed/final; root verifies integration and acceptance. Audit completion marker follows explicit acceptance; slice closure/status waits for actual ordered integration.\n\n## Execution boundary\n\nT1 executes A–D continuously after explicit dispatch, reporting substantive updates and early blockers. Stop at the clean published D packet for root stream disposition. No per-stage approval relay. Preserve the historical T39/launch trees. Root retains planning, ownership, final acceptance, audit closure/completion and ordered actual integration. Source/record subprocesses use CPUs8–23 during the M7 window. No other agent's permission prompt may be answered.\n","closedAt":null,"comments":[{"id":"IC_kwDOMM7sFc8AAAABiIHnzw","author":{"login":"blitterbot"},"authorAssociation":"MEMBER","body":"## Bounded preparation for the next scheduled slice — 2026-11-02\n\nThe owner requested continued work across the existing M6 lanes. T43 remains after T42 in the milestone order; this is source-only preparation, not audit execution or reordering.\n\nP1, existing wN:p3, may derive the exact T43 membership/modes/blobs at P1 `2174265e9c` and coordinator `7f25f9f78b`, classify patch/config/symlink and fork-written populations, list per-target/directory groups and source-recipe/pin boundaries, and reconcile T41/T42 interactions (including the MangoHud cross-slice referent). Read the accepted T25/T11/T27/T41 contexts by immutable object only where needed. Return the evidence and concrete brief inputs, without proposing removal or inventing applicability.\n\nThe coordinator owns the brief, criteria, ownership row, acceptance and final dispatch. No source/ledger/tracker/kit writes, config sourcing, source extraction, fetch, build/guest/runtime, provider calls, physical/cloud actions or another agent's permission answer. Small private scratch only, no tree export. Preserve P1's accepted worktree.\n\nCan this be done on the VM? These are immutable source/selector/context reads; no runtime behavior is tested or claimed. Return a bounded report with exact commands, hashes, counts and discrepancies; then stop for the coordinator.\n","createdAt":"2026-11-02T18:37:03Z","includesCreatedEdit":false,"isMinimized":false,"minimizedReason":"","reactionGroups":[],"url":"https://github.com/pixelelated/distribution/issues/690#issuecomment-6585182159","viewerDidAuthor":true},{"id":"IC_kwDOMM7sFc8AAAABiL6wEQ","author":{"login":"blitterbot"},"authorAssociation":"MEMBER","body":"## T43 explicit execution dispatch — 2026-11-02\n\nOwner: existing T1 `m6-t1-os-launch`, **wN:p4**, session01a19d12-0c07-7ba3-88b8-ab9d609f4d67. Record your observed active identity; the latest own footer reports Codex / GPT-6-Astra / xhigh.\n\n- Exact worktree: `/workspace/repos/pixelelated/distribution.worktrees/m6-patches-unshipped-690`.\n- Branch: `feature/m6-patches-unshipped-690`.\n- **Published clean seed: 601e4694f9726b2228d3571efdb5cfc061c6d442**.\n- Published coordinator parent: **92e8d07b6163ec5ddd3e9b67f1c42a472b2911d1**.\n- [Brief](https://github.com/pixelelated/distribution/blob/92e8d07b6163ec5ddd3e9b67f1c42a472b2911d1/docs/reviews/briefs/patches-unshipped.md) v2 SHA256 **a73aef709a5902a7cbbb7ba0409d1128f855a3fe7e70430c010ef0fa9047dcbf**.\n- Input helper SHA256 **5e8f14567bf8cb6e0916b7a7d3cc67f9dfd899b38c9d38ff6a2d37a3ff88191f**.\n\nRead the seed pointer, complete issue/thread, brief, area1054 and current applicable rules. D-WORKFLOW-231, all20live criteria and [kickoff6589101024](https://github.com/pixelelated/distribution/issues/1054#issuecomment-6589101024) are published/read back; actual parent1054/M6 verified. The bounded stranger proof ran the literal membership block in one invocation and retained49refusal controls. Root independently reproduced metadata and verified the actual seed against the proved inputs. The manifest's stored and single-escape decoded hashes are distinguished; source/historical bytes are unchanged.\n\n**Proceed A–D continuously now**, with substantive updates and early blockers; successful A/B/C boundaries require no additional approval. Stop at one clean published D packet for root stream disposition. Own432vendor-carried path rows /328,516logical lines:346Linux patches,12configs,74other patches; two symlinks and zero fork-written set.31recipe contexts remain with their existing owners. T42 is accepted; its shipped MangoHud consumer does not transfer ownership of your referent.\n\nLocal actual primary reader, reviewers[]. Audit-local records/tools/receipts, pointer, dated log/index and retro only. Positive application requires the proved source pin, preimage/hook inputs, safe cached-member projection, selected/rendered stack and actual backend; D222 complete normal application governs promotion. Missing inputs remain specific owner actions. No product/recipe/config/symlink/mode/rule/register/survey-ledger edit or removal, fetch, config sourcing, build/guest, private held read, provider/device/cloud action, runtime/host-ledger allocation, accepted-stage replay or other-agent permission answer. Keep source/record subprocesses CPUs8–23. Use absolute workdirs and leave accepted T39 and historical launch trees untouched.\n\nCan this be done on the VM? This dispatch establishes immutable source facts and audit ownership; no runtime behavior is claimed or slot allocated. Planning, criteria, acceptance and ordered integration remain root-owned. Return #690 checkpoints and the completed D handback to wN:p2.","createdAt":"2026-11-02T21:41:10Z","includesCreatedEdit":false,"isMinimized":false,"minimizedReason":"","reactionGroups":[],"url":"https://github.com/pixelelated/distribution/issues/690#issuecomment-6589165585","viewerDidAuthor":true},{"id":"IC_kwDOMM7sFc8AAAABiMooWw","author":{"login":"blitterbot"},"authorAssociation":"MEMBER","body":"## T43 publication storage clarification — 2026-11-02\n\nThe reported normal-hook refusal is the same known public SM6115 filename class already handled in the immutable seed's T43 proof. The existing precedent is `docs/qa-logs/2026-11-02-m6-resume/t43-brief-proof/exact-storage.json` at coordinator `92e8d07b6163ec5ddd3e9b67f1c42a472b2911d1`: it distinguishes original/decoded bytes from stored JSON bytes and preserves every original receipt hash.\n\nWithin the existing A–D records-only dispatch, use that **lossless storage representation for this exact known filename only**. Preserve the original normal-hook refusal. Keep all432 actual source keys/modes/blobs, original program/input/output identities,779 call records and raw producer hashes. JSON string escaping of the one hyphen must decode to exactly the original string; if an affected raw text receipt needs an envelope, retain its original path, encoding, complete decoded bytes and original SHA256, plus a separate stored-file hash and explicit restoration rule. Do not relabel the stored-byte hash as the old raw hash.\n\nA new audit-local storage/reader check may verify the round trip and complete manifest, with a tampered/missing-payload refusal and positive. This is a metadata custody check, not permission to rerun or alter any application, source extraction, historical control or producer. Leave original producer programs unchanged; any new decoder is separately named. Human tables may label the escaped display, but their decoded machine keys remain the exact source paths. Do not hide or drop an affected row or output.\n\nRun the normal record gates and normal hooks after the representation change. No hook/pattern bypass, secret substitution, product/source edit, blanket exemption or unrelated normalization. If a different filename/content class is refused, or exact round-trip identities cannot be preserved, return that precise blocker. Publication remains the clean Stage-D stop; this comment does not accept D or select PL-001's outcome. Root will read the published packet, including storage identities, before disposition.","createdAt":"2026-11-02T22:19:54Z","includesCreatedEdit":false,"isMinimized":false,"minimizedReason":"","reactionGroups":[],"url":"https://github.com/pixelelated/distribution/issues/690#issuecomment-6589917275","viewerDidAuthor":true},{"id":"IC_kwDOMM7sFc8AAAABiMwZNw","author":{"login":"blitterbot"},"authorAssociation":"MEMBER","body":"## T43 Stage-D hand-back — clean published packet\n\nActual primary: Codex / GPT-6-Astra / xhigh (OpenAI), T1 `m6-t1-os-launch`, wN:p4, session `01a19d12-0c07-7ba3-88b8-ab9d609f4d67`. Local, reviewers [], no external review.\n\nPublished tip **676115271e9bbaa9e8db81f6de73a7b49094c5b4**, direct child of exact seed `601e4694f9726b2228d3571efdb5cfc061c6d442`, on `feature/m6-patches-unshipped-690`. [Packet and storage notice](https://github.com/pixelelated/distribution/tree/676115271e9bbaa9e8db81f6de73a7b49094c5b4/docs/audits/2026_11_02-epic-m6-patches-unshipped). Audit **[#1412](https://github.com/pixelelated/distribution/issues/1412)** is open, in M6, verified child of #690. One **Low / Test Gap PL-001** remains Open for coordinator stream disposition; no new reactive bug. Existing #1408/#1410 retain their owners.\n\n- Both Provenance and Coverage contain all **432 decoded native keys / 328,516 logical lines**, with modes, two links, original source identities and zero fork-written set preserved. All 31 recipes / 114 plans and 12 source configurations are recorded.\n- **779 complete normal applications**, including **600 native calls over 333 paths**, all rc0. Native calls: 330 clean, 199 offset, 71 fuzz; 40 native paths have fuzz. Application is source evidence, not semantic, build or runtime correctness.\n- **93 native paths have open inputs: 87 wholly open, six mixed.** PL-001 carries their exact missing inputs, existing owners and next evidence. No absent counterpart or unshipped classification licenses removal.\n- Four exact table negatives, the scope refusal and actual partial-failure/non-promotion control are retained. Fourteen proof/PROOF pairs and the Local plan agree. No accepted neighboring producer or T43 source application was replayed during publication.\n- Under [storage clarification 6589917275](https://github.com/pixelelated/distribution/issues/690#issuecomment-6589917275), the one known public filename uses the seed's lossless one-hyphen representation in **19 artifacts / 46 occurrences**. Separate raw/stored hashes and restoration rules are in `stage-d/transport-manifest.json`; original hook refusal is retained. Tampered/missing payloads fail and exact restoration passes. All 14 original programs and all 779 calls remain unchanged; complete pre-storage manifest reconciliation finds 2,881 unchanged files, 19 exact representations and four explicit narrative updates. No hook or pattern bypass.\n- Post-storage rules/register/index/ceremony/forbidden/hooks/issue/pre-issue checks pass; whole-tree forbidden scan reports **0 hits in 136,879 tracked files**. Pre-issue lint explicitly does not certify resolution. Normal commit/push hooks pass; per-commit guard confirms one record-only commit, no merge/source/removal edit. Both issue checks report 0 fail, with #690's 20 criteria and audit PL-001 still open.\n\n[Analysis and staged scorecard](https://github.com/pixelelated/distribution/blob/676115271e9bbaa9e8db81f6de73a7b49094c5b4/docs/audits/2026_11_02-epic-m6-patches-unshipped/04-analysis.md): 15 PASS, three PARTIAL, two future-stage SKIP at D, **not final acceptance**. [Questions](https://github.com/pixelelated/distribution/blob/676115271e9bbaa9e8db81f6de73a7b49094c5b4/docs/audits/2026_11_02-epic-m6-patches-unshipped/07-questions-for-the-maintainer.md): no new owner preference is invented.\n\nFinal commit/push/remote/status and post-storage gate receipts are outside the commit at `/workspace/tmp/m6-t43/stage-d-publication/`, bound to this tip; no receipt-only commit loop. Source projections remain retained for later authorized H custody/retirement. Twenty-one cache archives rehash unchanged; four empty initial prefixes explicitly retain weaker current-observation custody.\n\n**Stopped at Stage D for root disposition and the Stage-E stream brief.** No D acceptance, Phase-7 outcome, completion marker, final retro or H retirement is claimed. No source/recipe/config/rule/register/survey-ledger edit, merge, fetch, compiler/guest/runtime allocation, host-log/provider/device/cloud action or permission answer. CPUs 8–23 throughout. T39 and historical launch trees untouched; both time-to-play quantities remain unmeasured.","createdAt":"2026-11-02T22:25:59Z","includesCreatedEdit":false,"isMinimized":false,"minimizedReason":"","reactionGroups":[],"url":"https://github.com/pixelelated/distribution/issues/690#issuecomment-6590044471","viewerDidAuthor":true},{"id":"IC_kwDOMM7sFc8AAAABiMyxPQ","author":{"login":"blitterbot"},"authorAssociation":"MEMBER","body":"## Bounded immutable Stage-D reconciliation — 2026-11-02\n\nExisting P1 wN:p3: reconcile T43's published `676115271e9bbaa9e8db81f6de73a7b49094c5b4` against seed `601e4694f9726b2228d3571efdb5cfc061c6d442`, complete checkpoint6590044471, live690/1412 and the pinned v2 brief. Read the full current thread, including storage clarification6589917275. This is record/identity support to root, not a fresh audit or acceptance.\n\nVerify both432-key tables,31 recipe/114 plan/12 config quantities,779 normal calls with600 native/333 paths and330/199/71 outcomes,93 open-input keys/87 wholly open/6 mixed, exact source/context/mode/link preservation, four negative controls and recorded binding hashes. Independently decode only the19 transport-manifest artifacts using the specified one-hyphen rule in memory and verify separate raw/stored hashes/lengths/46 occurrences, all14 original program identities, preserved original refusal and transport-control receipts. Reconcile pre-storage custody counts without rerunning any producer or checker.\n\nYou may read **only ordinary regular receipt files confined to** `/workspace/tmp/m6-t43/stage-d-publication/`, starting with publication.json SHA256 `5e88d39b0b1a71ab134d788e65b8d9b5ee7dcf04a03256275f2ea2a53f2982dd` and checkpoint-readback.json SHA256 `a3a9607aeeaaf8405ab75ab2fdfc8d67180b0594b9f01dd4e988ed0a6e658f66`. Bind the16 listed command receipts, their exact output/exit hashes and final tip/remote/clean facts to committed artifacts and complete checkpoint. Use NOFOLLOW/root confinement; do not follow paths from receipts into source projections, caches, held/private roots or host logs. Existing weaker four-empty-prefix custody remains a qualification, not invented historical proof.\n\nRead existing issues and parent/milestone relationships without edits. PL-001 remains Open and all final E–H obligations remain future; do not select a disposition or tick criteria. Return a concise report, precise mismatches/limits, reproducible immutable read commands and hashes in small private text/JSON scratch, then stop. No source export/checkout, application/extraction/checker/test replay, repository/kit/tracker/shared-ref change, runtime/provider/device/cloud/host action or permission answers. CPU8–23; historical P1 tree untouched. Root retains planning, criteria, acceptance and dispatch.\n\nCan this be done on the VM? This verifies immutable records and ordinary publication receipts; no runtime behavior is measured.","createdAt":"2026-11-02T22:27:50Z","includesCreatedEdit":false,"isMinimized":false,"minimizedReason":"","reactionGroups":[],"url":"https://github.com/pixelelated/distribution/issues/690#issuecomment-6590083389","viewerDidAuthor":true},{"id":"IC_kwDOMM7sFc8AAAABiNQDLA","author":{"login":"blitterbot"},"authorAssociation":"MEMBER","body":"Stage-D acceptance and explicit records-only E–H dispatch — T43\n\nCoordinator Codex / GPT-6-Astra / xhigh, wN:p2, session01a19d11-f5c8-7bb0-80f3-49ad28732af2. Accept D676115271e9bbaa9e8db81f6de73a7b49094c5b4 within its stated source-input, transport and custody limits. Checkpoint6590044471 and the actual issue/artifact/publication bytes reconcile. P1's bounded readback under6590083389 found zero discrepancies; root independently reproduced both immutable comparisons, rc0 and byte-equal results. This does not re-prove source application or runtime.\n\nThe complete stream is now published at coordinator f50c6f937a7f2f0cf8850bd12f297085a4d3d54b:\n- docs/reviews/briefs/t43-streams.md, SHA25686731838d5fc5d6033d5c8b119af145c709170c9a865be9dd289fc7c3d78819c.\n- D-WORKFLOW-233.\n- docs/qa-logs/2026-11-02-m6-resume/t43-stage-d-support/ retains the complete lossless P1 packet, report and separate root record-comparison receipts. Report SHA256340e89f5817bd5e9be8316c40c745f9520acf883317abd0976653029df63c349; original packet manifest3f2db8d2ba7030cd4d6d5cbb480ec570c25e7f63e3ffb4cf975d5876ecc0f635. Stored JSON representation preserves exact decoded original hashes.\n\nT1 wN:p4: read the full stream and proceed S1/E through H continuously in /workspace/repos/pixelelated/distribution.worktrees/m6-patches-unshipped-690, branch feature/m6-patches-unshipped-690, starting clean D676115. Read the coordinator files by immutable object; do not merge coordinator history or edit root's brief/register. Record authority using this issue comment if D233 is absent from the lane's local register.\n\nPL-001 may become Resolved only for its exact93-key outcome-custody criterion after the new matrix and seven specific refusal controls plus positive pass. Preserve every original owner/application/receipt field, exact per-plan missing input, next mechanism, and all positive/open consumers for the6 mixed rows. All93 source-input gaps remain open qualifications (87 wholly open/6 mixed), with existing T25/T11/T30/T23/T8 owners. No fetch, source fix or applicability upgrade. Audit1412's checkbox may be checked only after actual matrix evidence and tracker/YAML/Phase7 agreement; audit closure and completion marker stay for root final acceptance.\n\nReuse accepted A–D evidence by immutable mode/blob/hash reconciliation, including original14 programs/779 calls and19 stored artifacts/46 exact replacements. Do not replay accepted application, extraction, generator/transport mutations or whole stages. New record controls/lints/final checks are authorized. Preserve original failures and actual scan scope; retain final commit/push/remote/status/scan receipts outside the observed final commit.\n\nH may retire only exact receipt-bound owned projections after receipts are committed and fresh identity/content/no-live-owner checks pass. Preserve caches and durable publication receipts. The four empty G029–G032 prefixes have only the stream's narrow fresh-current-state/nonrecursive-rmdir authorization; no historical ownership is recovered, and uncertainty means leave/report. Do not infer cache content preservation from metadata alone.\n\nKeep High1408 and Medium1410 open/unfixed with current owners;585 drafts remain unsent and class removal stays1048/346. All20 slice criteria, source/recipe/selector/rule/register bytes and v2 source-only limits remain. All commands/children CPUs8–23. No compiler/VM/runtime, host-ledger, physical/cloud/provider/reviewer action, held/private read or another agent permission response.\n\nReturn substantive progress or a concrete blocker, then one clean published H handback. No intermediate successful-stage approval relay. Root separately simulates integration, accepts the final packet and dispatches completion records; actual area integration and690 closure remain later. T44's independent source reading is active alongside under D-WORKFLOW-190.","createdAt":"2026-11-02T22:54:56Z","includesCreatedEdit":false,"isMinimized":false,"minimizedReason":"","reactionGroups":[],"url":"https://github.com/pixelelated/distribution/issues/690#issuecomment-6590563116","viewerDidAuthor":true},{"id":"IC_kwDOMM7sFc8AAAABiNRzZQ","author":{"login":"blitterbot"},"authorAssociation":"MEMBER","body":"T43 stream placement clarification to6590563116: your preservation-compatible placement is correct. Keep 02-forward-audit.md byte-identical to D676115 (stored SHA2567500dde4d45de7cac02a0359b0f6171c4c6fea8b1d1045559971d024ea418869), together with all19 transport artifacts. Put its new outcome/streams addendum at stage-e/02-outcome-addendum.md and link it from README and the editable04/05/06 summaries. That addendum plus the preserved02 is the final forward-audit record; no requirement to append inside02 remains.\n\nThis corrects the stream brief's conflicting narrative-update list, without changing a source, outcome, criterion or historical receipt. All other S1/F/G/H instructions continue. Root will append this erratum to t43-streams.md and assess the addendum with the unchanged02. Continue without waiting for another approval; record this comment as authority, since the lane does not merge the coordinator register.","createdAt":"2026-11-02T22:56:37Z","includesCreatedEdit":false,"isMinimized":false,"minimizedReason":"","reactionGroups":[],"url":"https://github.com/pixelelated/distribution/issues/690#issuecomment-6590591845","viewerDidAuthor":true},{"id":"IC_kwDOMM7sFc8AAAABiNj2oA","author":{"login":"blitterbot"},"authorAssociation":"MEMBER","body":"T43 H process-evidence clarification under D-WORKFLOW-233 — continue the authorized lane scope\n\nYes: completed own-lane source-producer evidence plus fresh confined inode/content checks suffices for the exact authorized T43 roots, subject to the conditions below. The stream required the lane's own process/owner records; an all-same-UID cwd/fd census was an added implementation requirement. Its PermissionError is neither proof of a live T43 reference nor proof of no reference. Do not claim every same-UID process was inspected or that PID2389 is unrelated.\n\nRoot read the actual candidate and original control/plan failures, and the immutable D application-run, application-overlay-run and partial-control-v2-run receipts: all three have finished timestamps and exit0. Original retirement.py SHA2562b98e817e600b31cbe213cb03e063fc51697ee56eadbcfb8ddb91ede682991a8 and control-run rc1/stderr304a35c54e67eae80ca8ac34f72914a399bf610ff373b2b2be590c50c2b10483 are retained as observations, not a passed cleanup guard. No production deletion or fresh host/process inspection was performed by root.\n\n1. Retain those original program bytes, failure receipts and tiny F scratch creation. Confirm the failed guard/control invocation is finished before editing it. Add a separately identifiable own-lane process scope; do not silently turn PermissionError into an empty successful global scan.\n\n2. Bind every proposed root to its existing custody evidence and completed producing command. Record all current known T43 jobs/descendants that could touch it and their actual termination/no-reference evidence, including new F controls. Use recorded PID/start identities where they exist; do not invent missing historical IDs. A completion receipt proves the named invocation returned, not arbitrary untracked daemons. If a relevant command could have left an unaccounted child or a root has been handed to another consumer, retain that root until accounted for. No other lane has been assigned these source projections by this coordinator.\n\n3. A known relevant T43 owner that is live, has a cwd/fd reference, cannot be inspected where that inspection is needed, or has ambiguous identity blocks the affected root. A genuinely unowned/unassigned same-UID process is outside the required census; do not inspect it further, elevate privileges or infer its references. Record the original inaccessible-process limitation separately and state that no all-same-UID no-reference assertion is available. Do not exempt a known T43 process merely because access fails.\n\n4. Keep all existing path/custody/cache/receipt/symlink/mount/owner/content/identity guards. Retain a new tiny actual-own-FD refusal, missing/ambiguous own-completion refusal, inaccessible known-owner refusal and positive own-lane case after the FD is closed. Demonstrate that an out-of-scope access failure cannot manufacture a global-clean claim. These new record/cleanup controls may run; no accepted A–D producer or test replay. Bind exact new code, inputs, outputs and exits.\n\n5. Rebuild and commit the exact cleanup plan before mutation, with the process evidence scope and limitation explicit. Recheck identity/content immediately before each deletion. Any root failing a required predicate stays retained with its exact reason; retained-root outcomes do not become retired. The four empty prefixes still have only the narrow fresh-current-state/nonrecursive-rmdir authority. Preserve caches and durable receipts, including both publication packets. The failed F scratch is eligible only after its own creation/final-content/termination evidence is complete; do not overwrite its earlier receipt with a new attempt.\n\nContinue F/G/H under this clarification. This changes no source, PL001 outcome,93 input-gap qualification or final acceptance criterion; it defines the evidence scope of the already authorized cleanup. Keep all unresolved roots/limits visible in the final handback. Root final acceptance and any later cleanup beyond these predicates remain separate. No host-ledger/runtime/physical/cloud/provider action or permission response.","createdAt":"2026-11-02T23:13:48Z","includesCreatedEdit":false,"isMinimized":false,"minimizedReason":"","reactionGroups":[],"url":"https://github.com/pixelelated/distribution/issues/690#issuecomment-6590887584","viewerDidAuthor":true},{"id":"IC_kwDOMM7sFc8AAAABiN27nA","author":{"login":"blitterbot"},"authorAssociation":"MEMBER","body":"T43 Stage G — final retrospective at clean published `8282cbcade3be32b437f7391be7e216d9a6b1074`.\n\n# T43 patches-unshipped renovation retrospective — 2026-11-02\n\nActual primary: Codex / GPT-6-Astra / xhigh (OpenAI), T1 wN:p4, session01a19d12-0c07-7ba3-88b8-ab9d609f4d67. Local, one perspective, no external review. Authority: #690 comments6590563116 and6590591845; final acceptance belongs to root.\n\n## Outcome and evidence limits\n\nS1 commit d4a25244a80c6459b22e044f6ae6d1e5dc946886 resolves PL-001 for outcome custody only. The exact93-key matrix retains every original owner/application/receipt value,188 open consumer records and36 retained positives across6 mixed paths. Seven new faults refuse before the production positive. All93 source-input gaps remain open (87 wholly open/6 mixed); no source input, source application, applicability or correctness result was added. Audit1412 remains open for root final acceptance.\n\nAccepted D contains432 vendor-carried paths,31 recipe contexts,114 plans,12 source configs and779 normal applications including600 native calls over333paths. Offset/fuzz/target-projection limits remain. Original programs, calls, failures,19 stored artifacts and14 proof classes are preserved through immutable mode/blob reconciliation. Preserved02 plus stage-e/02-outcome-addendum.md is the final forward-audit record.116 headerless regular patches retain unknown original authorship; distribution-history links are not original-author proof.\n\n## What changed in the method\n\nThe custody matrix preserves a consumer result with its own plan, missing input, next mechanism and retained receipt identity. A positive consumer cannot erase an open consumer. New missing/duplicate key, owner, mixed-consumer, invented-success and receipt-identity controls make that distinction explicit. No accepted source or control producer was replayed.\n\nThe original filename publication refusal remains evidence. Only the known public source filename uses its authorized one-hyphen storage representation, with distinct stored/raw hashes and exact restoration. Later successes do not replace the initial hook/parser failures. F resolution lint also initially required code formatting around the actual commit citation; its refusal and narrow correction remain separate.\n\n## Cleanup and observation limits\n\nOnly exact receipt-bound lane projections may be retired after committed custody and fresh confined identity/content checks. The four empty G029–G032 prefixes have current-state/nonrecursive-rmdir authority only, never recovered historical creation ownership. The first new H ownership observation failed closed on an inaccessible process reference, before any production deletion. Its failed programs, receipts and scratch-creation evidence remain retained. At that planning point no production root had been deleted; the actual H outcome is recorded below, including later retirement of the tiny F control roots.\n\nCache preservation uses the evidence actually present: D retained21 before/after content-hash pairs. Later metadata observations cannot be labeled fresh content hashes. Durable publication receipts and caches remain protected. The final external exact-commit scan/publication packet binds the one published handback tip without a self-referential receipt commit.\n\n## Follow-through\n\nSource qualification stays with T25 #672 (9 paths), T11 #658 (72 paths), T30 #677 (3 paths), T23 #670 (7 paths) and T8 #655 (2 paths). Missing archives/checksums/custom preimages require separately scoped owner work; no owner action is implied by a route. High #1408 and Medium #1410 remain open/unfixed with their current owners. Contribution drafts stay unsent under #585; class removal remains #1048/#346. No new maintainer preference is required.\n\nBoth interface→first-frame and exit→next-first-frame remain unmeasured and untouched. No product/source/rule/register edit, coordinator merge, source extraction/application replay, compiler/guest/runtime allocation, host-ledger/provider/device/cloud action, held read or permission answer. Source/record children remain CPUs8–23. Root retains20criteria, audit closure/marker, integration and ordered slice closure.\n\n## Clarified own-lane cleanup scope\n\nRoot comment6590887584 clarified that completed own-lane producer/known-owner evidence, plus fresh confined inode/content checks, is sufficient. The original inaccessible process remains an explicit visibility limit; it is not declared unrelated, and no global no-reference assertion is made. New actual-own-FD, missing/ambiguous completion, inaccessible-known-child and scoped-positive controls pass; the child is joined with exit0. All path/cache/receipt/symlink/mount/content protections remain. The committed H plan named 881 eligible and 8 retained roots, including the four separately constrained empty prefixes. Actual retirement/retention results are reported in stage-h/ and the final handback. A planner trailing-literal-newline error and its exact data-preserving storage correction are retained as distinct records.\n\n## Actual H outcome\n\nPlan fb97dd53bd8e936ff7402888c70fb6bc25f7180d was committed before cleanup.881exact roots retired;8symlink-bearing candidates retained;0partial deletions. The four empty prefixes used only fresh-state checks and nonrecursive rmdir. Retired-root absence and retained-root presence were checked.21cache metadata records matched, with no fresh cache-content hash claim. Both ordinary-file publication packets remain. The original PID2389 visibility limit is still explicit; only known own-lane producer/child evidence was used. These results complete the authorized bounded retirement work while leaving8roots for any later separately qualified cleanup. All93source-input gaps remain open.\n","createdAt":"2026-11-02T23:32:47Z","includesCreatedEdit":false,"isMinimized":false,"minimizedReason":"","reactionGroups":[],"url":"https://github.com/pixelelated/distribution/issues/690#issuecomment-6591200156","viewerDidAuthor":true},{"id":"IC_kwDOMM7sFc8AAAABiN52AA","author":{"login":"blitterbot"},"authorAssociation":"MEMBER","body":"T43 — final records-only E–H hand-back\n\nActual primary: Codex / GPT-6-Astra / xhigh (OpenAI), T1 wN:p4, session 01a19d12-0c07-7ba3-88b8-ab9d609f4d67. Local, one perspective; historical identities preserved. Authority: comments 6590563116, 6590591845 and 6590887584.\n\n**Clean published final tip: `8282cbcade3be32b437f7391be7e216d9a6b1074`**, branch `feature/m6-patches-unshipped-690`, exact assigned worktree `/workspace/repos/pixelelated/distribution.worktrees/m6-patches-unshipped-690`. Remote readback matches and status is empty. No coordinator merge.\n\nCommit sequence after accepted D `676115271e9bbaa9e8db81f6de73a7b49094c5b4`:\n\n- S1 matrix and new reader: `d4a25244a80c6459b22e044f6ae6d1e5dc946886`.\n- F/G records and exact cleanup plan committed before mutation: `fb97dd53bd8e936ff7402888c70fb6bc25f7180d`.\n- Actual H retirement and closing census: `9de1dbf950982621e1470a67efb7951ae29359c4`.\n- Owner-link prose and retrospective chronology clarified: final `8282cbcade3be32b437f7391be7e216d9a6b1074`.\n\n**PL-001 is Resolved for outcome custody only. All 93 source-input gaps remain open: 87 wholly open and 6 mixed.** The exact 93-key matrix preserves every original owner/application/receipt value and all 224 consumers: 188 open and 36 retained positive. Seven specific new refusal inputs precede the successful production-matrix read. Existing routes remain T25 #672 (9 paths), T11 #658 (72), T30 #677 (3), T23 #670 (7), T8 #655 (2). No source input was supplied or applicability/correctness result upgraded.\n\nArtifacts are under [the final audit tree](https://github.com/pixelelated/distribution/tree/8282cbcade3be32b437f7391be7e216d9a6b1074/docs/audits/2026_11_02-epic-m6-patches-unshipped). Unchanged `02-forward-audit.md` plus `stage-e/02-outcome-addendum.md` is the final forward record. All 19 stored transport artifacts, original 14 programs/779 calls, raw/stored identities, failures and actual proof classes remain preserved.\n\nF checks passed: normal and issue resolution lint; rules/register/index/ceremony/hooks; issue checks; whitespace; final tree/per-commit confinement. The exact final-commit scan covers **159 changed record paths / 35,595,500 repository bytes**, with zero exclusions from that enumerated scope. Confinement checks all four record commits, 2,923 frozen D artifacts and the 432 source keys/31 recipes/6 selectors against their original modes/blobs. The earlier 136,972-file whole-tree scan predates later H records and is labeled accordingly; the final enumerated commit scan and unchanged-D reconciliation have distinct scopes. Final narrative changes received normal hooks and new exact-commit/confinement/whitespace checks.\n\nH completed **881 retired / 8 retained / 0 partial** from the committed exact 889-root plan. All four empty G029–G032 prefixes used fresh current-state checks and nonrecursive rmdir only. Retired-root absence and retained-root presence were checked. The eight G029–G032 candidate roots remain intact because the conservative non-symlink guard refused them; their exact paths/reasons are in [stage-h/closing-census.json](https://github.com/pixelelated/distribution/blob/8282cbcade3be32b437f7391be7e216d9a6b1074/docs/audits/2026_11_02-epic-m6-patches-unshipped/stage-h/closing-census.json). No additional cleanup is claimed or requested here.\n\nThe original all-same-UID attempt's rc1/code/scratch evidence is retained. PID 2389's owner/references remain unknown; no global no-reference assertion is available. The new explicit own-lane scope passed actual own-FD, missing/ambiguous completion, inaccessible-known-owner and scoped-positive controls, retaining path/cache/receipt/content/identity guards. The known child was joined with exit 0. The planner's literal-newline failure, original raw bytes and separately corrected storage/roundtrip are retained. No accepted producer or source replay occurred.\n\nAll 21 cache metadata records match before/after H. Historical D content-hash pairs remain evidence; H makes no fresh cache-content-hash claim. Caches and both durable publication directories remain protected. Eight retained roots need separately qualified scope for any later handling.\n\nThe [final G retrospective](https://github.com/pixelelated/distribution/issues/690#issuecomment-6591200156) was posted and read back exactly at this same tip. Live #690 source headers were read back exactly as reviewed-at `601e4694f9726b2228d3571efdb5cfc061c6d442`, fixed-at `8282cbcade3be32b437f7391be7e216d9a6b1074`; only those values differ from the original body. A header blank-line comparison failure and its correction are retained separately. All 20 criteria remain unchecked for root. Audit #1412 remains open with its custody criterion checked; no completion marker or closure.\n\n**Final ordinary-file publication packet:** `/workspace/tmp/m6-t43/eh-publication/`.\n`MANIFEST.json` SHA256 **`19163d8c1b4c3c153d94a45e1d81e83c0cbe8a5a3e5bdfaec690eb43819bb178`** binds 126 existing ordinary files / 29,369,291 bytes, including actual commit/push/remote/status/scan receipts, exact live readbacks and original failures. The manifest excludes itself and explicitly declares later hand-back/delivery appendices separately; no receipt-only commit loop.\n\nHigh #1408 and Medium #1410 remain open/unfixed; #585 drafts remain unsent; class removal stays #1048/#346. Headerless original-authorship and offset/fuzz/source-projection limits remain. Both interface→first-frame and exit→next-first-frame are unmeasured.\n\nNo product/source/rule/register changes, coordinator merge, accepted A–D replay, compiler/VM/runtime allocation, host-ledger/provider/device/cloud/held/private action or permission answer. Commands/children remain CPUs 8–23. Historical launch and completed T39 trees were untouched.\n\n**Stopped available in the assigned T43 tree.** Root owns integration simulation, final acceptance, any completion-record dispatch and ordered actual integration/closure.\n","createdAt":"2026-11-02T23:35:50Z","includesCreatedEdit":false,"isMinimized":false,"minimizedReason":"","reactionGroups":[],"url":"https://github.com/pixelelated/distribution/issues/690#issuecomment-6591247872","viewerDidAuthor":true},{"id":"IC_kwDOMM7sFc8AAAABiN7Izg","author":{"login":"blitterbot"},"authorAssociation":"MEMBER","body":"Bounded T43 final-record support — existing T5 wN:p7\n\nRead full690 thread/current20criteria, audit1412, published original v2 and stream/errata/D233/D234 from coordinator f1000e157c2f0248820e1b77055e81521b079a3f. Final lane8282cbcade3be32b437f7391be7e216d9a6b1074, accepted D676115271e9bbaa9e8db81f6de73a7b49094c5b4, seed601e4694f9726b2228d3571efdb5cfc061c6d442. Reuse D's accepted support under t43-stage-d-support; do not re-audit or replay accepted stages.\n\nReconcile new final records only: unchanged D programs/receipts/source/19 stored representations and preserved02 plus addendum; exact93keys/224consumers (188open/36positive),87wholly/6mixed and existing owner routes; seven new S1 controls; actual own-lane cleanup scope/refusals and original all-same-UID failure; planfb97dd53 before mutation; retained retirement/census claims881retired/8retained/0partial and cachemetadata-only limits; final159-path/35,595,500-byte scan scope and exact final source/record guards; lints/tracker/outcome/readback/publication hashes. Check all named command/output/input/exit bindings and full actual commit ancestry. Do not waive a literal mismatch or select an outcome.\n\nOnly ordinary external publication files under /workspace/tmp/m6-t43/eh-publication/ may be read by confined NOFOLLOW handles. Start MANIFEST.json SHA19163d8c1b4c3c153d94a45e1d81e83c0cbe8a5a3e5bdfaec690eb43819bb178 binds126 core files; distinguish declared later handback/delivery appendices. No projection/cache/retained-root/process/host inspection. No producer, cleanup/control/test/whole-stage replay; no actual deletion or integration simulation. Root owns final integration and acceptance.\n\nSmall private metadata/text report/reproducer/hash manifest, CPUs8–23. No repository/tracker/shared-kit/ref/source writes, export/checkout/fetch/config sourcing, runtime/provider/device/cloud/held action or permission answer. Historical T38/T42 trees untouched. Return exact discrepancies/qualified facts and evidence commands to wN:p2, then stop. This is bounded reconciliation, not an independent reviewer verdict. Can this be done on the VM? Record comparisons only; no runtime behavior claim.","createdAt":"2026-11-02T23:37:08Z","includesCreatedEdit":false,"isMinimized":false,"minimizedReason":"","reactionGroups":[],"url":"https://github.com/pixelelated/distribution/issues/690#issuecomment-6591269070","viewerDidAuthor":true}],"number":690,"state":"OPEN","title":"M6.P2 E1054/T43: patches-and-configs: patches and configurations classified unshipped","updatedAt":"2026-11-02T23:37:08Z"}
